EXT. MOUNTAIN PASS - SNOWBOUND BUS - DAY

A stalled coach bus lists on a white slope, wheels buried to the axles. Wind hisses across the frozen glass. Pines bend under the weight of snow.

Inside, a dim cabin. Frost on the windows. Seven seats cleared in a tight circle near the driver's cab.

KIT, 40s, a nurse in a puffy coat, rubs a young girl's hands. BERNARD, 60s, a retired surveyor with a thick gray scarf, studies a folded map. YARA, 20s, a student with a backpack, shivers in her sleeping bag. LARS, 50s, the bus driver, in his uniform jacket, works a hand-crank radio. PILAR, 30s, a mother, holds a thermos of soup between her palms. They are all gaunt, hollow-eyed, patient.

KIT
Everyone drink something.

BERNARD
We're low on water.

KIT
We have snow.

LARS
Snow takes heat to melt.

YARA
Then we burn something.

BERNARD
We burned the seat covers yesterday.

PILAR
(to herself)
Hold on, hold on.

LARS
(cranking)
Come on, you old brute.

The radio coughs. A thin, tinny voice breaks through.

RADIO (V.O.)
(garbled)
-- anyone -- copy --

Everyone freezes. Lars twists the dial.

LARS
This is the Valmont Pass bus, number twelve. We're stranded at mile forty. Do you read?

RADIO (V.O.)
(garbled)
-- stay put -- help -- morning --

LARS
Say again?

The signal dies. Lars slumps. Pilar clutches the thermos.

KIT
Morning. That's something.

YARA
Whose morning?

BERNARD
Don't start.

Kit pulls her glove off and checks the girl's pulse at the wrist. The girl, who has not spoken, turns her head toward the door.

The bus door hisses open. A gust of snow sweeps in. A figure stands in the stairwell, bundled in white, a rifle slung over one shoulder: TOBIAS, 40s, a ranger, ice crusted on his beard.

TOBIAS
Got your signal. I'm Tobias. I'm here to get you out.

Nobody moves. Then Pilar lets out a sob. Kit rises. Bernard folds the map.

LARS
How many of you?

TOBIAS
Just me. Sled's at the bottom. Two trips.

KIT
She goes first.

TOBIAS
Who?

KIT
(gesturing)
Her. And she goes with her.

Pilar nods. She stands, takes the girl's hand, and moves to the door.
